.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_ALGOR_DUP 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_ALGOR_dup ,
.Nm X509_ALGOR_set0 ,
.Nm X509_ALGOR_get0 ,
.Nm X509_ALGOR_set_md ,
.Nm X509_ALGOR_cmp ,
.Nm X509_ALGOR_copy
.Nd AlgorithmIdentifier functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft X509_ALGOR *
.Fo X509_ALGOR_dup
.Fa "X509_ALGOR *alg"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ALGOR_set0
.Fa "X509_ALGOR *alg"
.Fa "ASN1_OBJECT *aobj"
.Fa "int ptype"
.Fa "void *pval"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo X509_ALGOR_get0
.Fa "const ASN1_OBJECT **paobj"
.Fa "int *pptype"
.Fa "const void **ppval"
.Fa "const X509_ALGOR *alg"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo X509_ALGOR_set_md
.Fa "X509_ALGOR *alg"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ALGOR_cmp
.Fa "const X509_ALGOR *a"
.Fa "const X509_ALGOR *b"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ALGOR_copy
.Fa "X509_ALGOR *dest"
.Fa "const X509_ALGOR *src"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_ALGOR_dup
returns a copy of
.Fa alg .
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_set0
sets the algorithm OID of
.Fa alg
to
.Fa aobj
and the associated parameter type to
.Fa ptype
with value
.Fa pval .
If
.Fa ptype
is
.Sy V_ASN1_UNDEF
the parameter is omitted, otherwise
.Fa ptype
and
.Fa pval
have the same meaning as the
.Em type
and
.Em value
parameters to
.Xr ASN1_TYPE_set 3 .
All the supplied parameters are used internally so must
.Sy NOT
be freed after this call succeeded; otherwise ownership remains with the
caller and
.Fa alg
remains untouched.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_get0
is the inverse of
.Fn X509_ALGOR_set0 :
it returns the algorithm OID in
.Em *paobj
and the associated parameter in
.Em *pptype
and
.Em *ppval
from the
.Sy AlgorithmIdentifier
.Fa alg .
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_set_md
sets the
.Sy AlgorithmIdentifier
.Fa alg
to appropriate values for the message digest
.Fa md .
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_cmp
compares
.Fa a
and
.Fa b
and returns 0 if they have identical encodings and nonzero otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_copy
copies the source values into the dest structs; making a duplicate of
each (and free any thing pointed to from within *dest).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_ALGOR_dup
returns a valid
.Vt X509_ALGOR
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_set0
and
.Fn X509_ALGOR_copy
return 1 on success or 0 on error.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_get0
and
.Fn X509_ALGOR_set_md
return no values.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ALGOR_cmp
returns 0 if the two parameters have identical encodings and nonzero
otherwise.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn X509_ALGOR_copy
was added in 1.1.1e.
